00:30:44.480 --> 00:30:45.880
I noticed it as well.

803
00:30:46.020 --> 00:30:46.340
Mm-hmm.

804
00:30:46.720 --> 00:30:48.180
So I looked in the script.

805
00:30:48.320 --> 00:30:55.340
I wanted to see if there was a script note about Jim's flower arrangement to Pam.

806
00:30:55.340 --> 00:30:59.780
I want to hear it because I have a theory that I will prove.

807
00:30:59.980 --> 00:31:01.400
I think I can prove it.

808
00:31:01.660 --> 00:31:01.920
Okay.

809
00:31:02.240 --> 00:31:04.140
Here is what the script said.

810
00:31:04.360 --> 00:31:05.380
There was a note.

811
00:31:06.200 --> 00:31:12.020
There is a small bouquet of non-rose flowers on Pam's desk.

812
00:31:12.360 --> 00:31:12.880
Okay.

813
00:31:13.620 --> 00:31:19.640
Well, I think Phil Shea from Props ran with this because later in the episode, when they

814
00:31:19.640 --> 00:31:24.820
go to the fancy restaurant with Bob and Phyllis, the same arrangement is on all the tables.

815
00:31:25.340 --> 00:31:25.580
Really?

816
00:31:25.860 --> 00:31:26.240
Yes.

817
00:31:26.460 --> 00:31:32.380
And if you look up cheap flowers for big events, carnations and daisies, if you have an event,

818
00:31:32.520 --> 00:31:35.540
like a wedding or whatever, they help fill out the arrangements.

819
00:31:35.760 --> 00:31:38.160
So I think Phil was like, okay, great.

820
00:31:38.440 --> 00:31:44.680
I can get this small bouquet of the same arrangement that I'm doing for the dinner at the restaurant.

821
00:31:45.140 --> 00:31:45.500
Yeah.

822
00:31:46.220 --> 00:31:51.040
So in Jim's defense, I don't know, maybe it helped out our props department.

823
00:31:51.360 --> 00:31:57.040
Well, I'll also have you know, in the same scene at three minutes and 17 seconds, my grocery list is gone.

824
00:31:57.680 --> 00:32:00.040
So we obviously shot this on a different day.

825
00:32:00.320 --> 00:32:00.680
Yeah.

826
00:32:00.680 --> 00:32:01.800
And I've been shopping now.

827
00:32:01.960 --> 00:32:03.900
So in case you were worried, I got all my stuff.

828
00:32:04.180 --> 00:32:05.580
Michael does not like the flowers.

829
00:32:05.840 --> 00:32:06.020
No.

830
00:32:06.140 --> 00:32:06.760
He's not a fan.

831
00:32:06.800 --> 00:32:07.720
He puts them on the floor.

832
00:32:07.860 --> 00:32:08.100
He puts them on the floor.

833
00:32:08.200 --> 00:32:09.140
He doesn't want to see them.

834
00:32:09.340 --> 00:32:10.320
I was like, you know what?

835
00:32:10.320 --> 00:32:11.840
I get that he doesn't want to see them.

836
00:32:12.060 --> 00:32:16.040
The floor, couldn't he just like put them like on one of those tables behind her?

837
00:32:16.160 --> 00:32:16.600
I don't know.

838
00:32:16.680 --> 00:32:17.620
He wouldn't be able to see them.

839
00:32:18.120 --> 00:32:21.300
Well, he goes up to Jim and he says, I need to have a word with you.

840
00:32:22.100 --> 00:32:26.240
And he says that today is a very difficult day for many people in the office.

841
00:32:26.700 --> 00:32:32.040
And that Pam and Jim's sexy vibes are creating a hostile work environment.

842
00:32:32.400 --> 00:32:34.500
This whole conversation made me laugh so hard.

843
00:32:34.620 --> 00:32:36.780
First of all, it's kind of in hushed tones, you know?

844
00:32:36.780 --> 00:32:39.760
And they're saying ridiculous things in hushed tones.

845
00:32:39.920 --> 00:32:41.320
That was always really hard for me.

846
00:32:41.800 --> 00:32:45.860
And when you're like, Michael, you do not get to be in our relationship.

847
00:32:47.240 --> 00:32:53.640
Lady, I wrote that down because I remember making a choice to say that as if it's not

848
00:32:53.640 --> 00:32:55.580
the first time I've had to explain it to Michael.

849
00:32:55.580 --> 00:32:56.160
It was really good.

850
00:32:56.160 --> 00:32:57.640
I wanted it to have history.

851
00:32:57.880 --> 00:32:58.300
It did.

852
00:32:58.480 --> 00:32:59.500
It really paid off.

853
00:32:59.720 --> 00:33:04.640
Well, we had a fan question from Maddie L who says, when Michael asks Jim to have

854
00:33:04.640 --> 00:33:08.300
a word with him, he starts to stand up as if he's going to head to Michael's office,

855
00:33:08.500 --> 00:33:12.840
but then awkwardly sits back down when Michael chooses to sit on Jim's desk instead.

856
00:33:13.180 --> 00:33:14.860
Was this improvised?

857
00:33:15.000 --> 00:33:16.260
I think it was.

858
00:33:16.340 --> 00:33:18.980
I looked in the script to see if there was any...

859
00:33:18.980 --> 00:33:20.180
Stage direction.

860
00:33:20.440 --> 00:33:22.100
Yeah, there wasn't.

861
00:33:22.160 --> 00:33:24.860
Except that it clearly says they don't move into Michael's office.

862
00:33:25.020 --> 00:33:26.100
They stay at Jim's desk.

863
00:33:26.260 --> 00:33:29.960
So I think that feels like something that John and Steve probably found in the moment.

864
00:33:30.100 --> 00:33:30.960
It's very funny.

865
00:33:30.960 --> 00:33:31.900
A hundred percent.

866
00:33:32.140 --> 00:33:34.780
And I feel like those guys, you know, we've talked about this a lot.

867
00:33:34.900 --> 00:33:37.780
By this time, everyone knew their characters so well.

868
00:33:37.960 --> 00:33:42.360
So those tops and bottoms of a scene, you could kind of play around a little bit.

869
00:33:42.560 --> 00:33:44.740
And it looked like them just having fun.

870
00:33:45.400 --> 00:33:47.580
It's time to talk about Dwight.

871
00:33:49.180 --> 00:33:51.340
I feel like Dwight...

872
00:33:52.120 --> 00:33:53.140
How do I say this?

873
00:33:53.720 --> 00:33:57.800
I feel like this episode really shows so much of who Dwight is.

874
00:33:58.360 --> 00:34:03.780
There's deleted scenes where he talks about the bloodmobile being a vampire magnet after dark.

875
00:34:04.220 --> 00:34:06.720
He's ready for anything and everything, you know?

876
00:34:07.460 --> 00:34:07.960
Yes.

877
00:34:08.160 --> 00:34:11.680
And he has a lot of stuff to share about how his body can do things.

878
00:34:12.180 --> 00:34:12.680
Yes.

879
00:34:13.060 --> 00:34:17.440
The nurse is trying to take blood, but she can't find a vein.

880
00:34:17.900 --> 00:34:19.100
Well, you know why?

881
00:34:19.360 --> 00:34:20.660
He's hidden it from her.

882
00:34:21.340 --> 00:34:24.020
And when he's ready, he's going to pop it on out for her.

883
00:34:24.240 --> 00:34:24.400
Yeah.

884
00:34:24.400 --> 00:34:30.800
Then he has a talking head where he tells us he can also retract his penis up into himself.

885
00:34:31.020 --> 00:34:31.220
Yeah.

886
00:34:31.380 --> 00:34:35.580
He says, I train my major blood vessels to retract into my body on command.

887
00:34:35.920 --> 00:34:38.720
Also, I can retract my penis up into itself.

888
00:34:39.000 --> 00:34:41.000
We had a fan question from Robin T.

889
00:34:41.220 --> 00:34:42.280
Robin, go.

890
00:34:42.760 --> 00:34:49.100
Dwight's lines about retracting his blood vessels and penis is one of my favorite quotes from the entire show.

891
00:34:49.100 --> 00:34:53.580
It is so absolutely absurd and hilarious and so very Dwight.

892
00:34:53.720 --> 00:34:56.460
I want to know everything about this line.

893
00:34:56.740 --> 00:34:58.220
Was it scripted?

894
00:34:58.520 --> 00:35:00.340
How hard was it to get through?

895
00:35:00.940 --> 00:35:05.020
I'll tell you, it was scripted, but this was an alternate talking head.

896
00:35:05.100 --> 00:35:07.560
This is not the one that appeared in our shooting draft.

897
00:35:07.780 --> 00:35:13.200
So, I wasn't there when they shot it, but I have to imagine it was very difficult to get through.

898
00:35:13.760 --> 00:35:16.360
Well, it's Michael's turn to give blood, guys.

899
00:35:16.660 --> 00:35:18.400
Wow, that's a big needle, he says.

900
00:35:18.400 --> 00:35:20.020
Are you squeamish around needles?

901
00:35:20.700 --> 00:35:25.380
I can give blood, I don't get faint or anything, but I don't like to watch it.

902
00:35:25.660 --> 00:35:26.000
Yeah.

903
00:35:26.060 --> 00:35:32.680
I don't like to see the needle go in my arm, I don't like to see the bag fill up, but I don't like it faint or weird around blood.

904
00:35:33.040 --> 00:35:33.580
Yeah, yeah.

905
00:35:33.580 --> 00:35:36.120
If someone's bleeding, it doesn't make me faint.

906
00:35:36.360 --> 00:35:37.060
Yeah, same, same.

907
00:35:37.240 --> 00:35:37.460
Okay.

908
00:35:37.940 --> 00:35:46.200
Michael, on the other hand, is very nervous, but luckily, there's a lovely young woman also giving blood and they start joking around.

909
00:35:46.740 --> 00:35:47.220
Yes.

910
00:35:47.220 --> 00:35:50.440
We asked Katie about this scene.

911
00:35:50.600 --> 00:35:59.160
I wanted to know, did she do any research into the process of giving blood and all of that?

912
00:35:59.160 --> 00:36:00.540
And here's what she had to say.

913
00:36:00.540 --> 00:36:12.880
I didn't do any research for this role, but I didn't need to because my character was just nervous and pleasant.

914
00:36:12.880 --> 00:36:17.980
And I didn't have to dig super deep to access those emotions.

915
00:36:18.220 --> 00:36:34.600
But the funny, I do have a very funny anecdote about being nervous or my character being nervous is that my first line was me just laughing nervously and saying, I'm so sorry.

916
00:36:34.600 --> 00:36:35.680
I'm so nervous.

917
00:36:36.280 --> 00:36:36.780
I'm so nervous.

918
00:36:36.780 --> 00:36:40.460
And Steve kept cutting.

919
00:36:40.820 --> 00:36:43.280
And he would be like, oh, no, it's okay.

920
00:36:43.300 --> 00:36:44.040
We'll go again.

921
00:36:44.200 --> 00:36:44.880
We'll go again.

922
00:36:45.000 --> 00:36:48.420
And finally, I was just like, I think it's my line.

923
00:36:48.420 --> 00:36:54.200
I think that's what I'm supposed to say, but that has always made me laugh.

924
00:36:54.300 --> 00:36:57.480
And of course, yes, I was thrilled to work with Steve.

925
00:36:57.680 --> 00:37:02.240
To get that – to get the show was its own triumph.

926
00:37:02.240 --> 00:37:07.260
But then to have my scene be with him was just like I was over the moon.

927
00:37:08.720 --> 00:37:13.540
I love that story about Steve because he was such a caretaker like that.

928
00:37:13.700 --> 00:37:16.640
He would want our guest actors to feel really comfortable.

929
00:37:17.100 --> 00:37:18.620
And he'd be like, oh, no, it's okay.

930
00:37:18.620 --> 00:37:19.440
We'll start again.

931
00:37:19.620 --> 00:37:20.700
We'll wait until you're comfortable.

932
00:37:20.980 --> 00:37:22.800
I was like, no, it's actually my line.

933
00:37:23.500 --> 00:37:29.640
I would also be relieved if the first time I ever had to be in a scene with Steve, I got to just laugh nervously and say I was nervous.

934
00:37:29.740 --> 00:37:30.080
Yes.

935
00:37:30.480 --> 00:37:31.980
Because it would be so truthful.

936
00:37:32.240 --> 00:37:33.760
Such an honest moment.

937
00:37:34.000 --> 00:37:34.120
Yeah.

938
00:37:34.600 --> 00:37:36.340
There's a third person in this scene.

939
00:37:36.540 --> 00:37:37.560
It's the nurse.

940
00:37:37.780 --> 00:37:38.880
She was great.

941
00:37:39.200 --> 00:37:43.220
I wondered if she was a real bloodmobile nurse since that was a real bloodmobile.

942
00:37:43.400 --> 00:37:46.820
Yeah, and she seemed kind of no-nonsense, like very comfortable there.

943
00:37:47.020 --> 00:37:48.800
Well, she was, in fact, an actress.

944
00:37:49.100 --> 00:37:50.580
Her name is Julie Ramallah.

945
00:37:51.060 --> 00:37:59.340
She has not been on Monk or Law and Order, but she was on several episodes of The Young and the Restless as well as many movies and TV shows.

946
00:37:59.340 --> 00:38:02.280
Well, Michael's going to make the mistake of looking at his blood bag.

947
00:38:02.600 --> 00:38:03.800
He freaks out a little.

948
00:38:04.080 --> 00:38:05.660
And he says to her, tell me stories.

949
00:38:05.800 --> 00:38:06.160
Say something.

950
00:38:06.360 --> 00:38:06.940
Distract me.

951
00:38:07.460 --> 00:38:08.980
And she says he's cute.

952
00:38:09.540 --> 00:38:09.940
Mm-hmm.

953
00:38:14.520 --> 00:38:17.320
Mm-hmm.

954
00:38:17.320 --> 00:38:18.440
And he passes out.

955
00:38:18.960 --> 00:38:19.260
Yes.

956
00:38:19.480 --> 00:38:20.460
We had a fan question.

957
00:38:20.820 --> 00:38:27.000
Many, many people wanted to know, how do we do these scenes of people giving blood?

958
00:38:27.280 --> 00:38:29.920
Some people wanted to know, did they actually give blood?

959
00:38:30.100 --> 00:38:30.560
No.

960
00:38:30.560 --> 00:38:31.580
Oh, my goodness.

961
00:38:31.760 --> 00:38:32.080
No.

962
00:38:32.540 --> 00:38:32.800
You know.

963
00:38:32.920 --> 00:38:33.760
Not in the episode.

964
00:38:34.100 --> 00:38:37.040
Yes, the next day, but not while we were filming.

965
00:38:37.900 --> 00:38:41.840
The next day with trained professionals and not actors pretending to take blood.

966
00:38:41.980 --> 00:38:42.280
Correct.

967
00:38:42.980 --> 00:38:46.180
I found out how they make fakie blood.

968
00:38:46.820 --> 00:38:47.340
Oh.

969
00:38:47.820 --> 00:38:49.220
Thanks to Randy Cordray.

970
00:38:49.420 --> 00:38:50.460
How do they do it?

971
00:38:50.700 --> 00:38:51.100
All right.

972
00:38:51.100 --> 00:38:57.680
It's a combination of water, food coloring, and you're not going to believe it.

973
00:38:58.800 --> 00:38:59.620
One more thing.

974
00:39:00.280 --> 00:39:00.820
Wait, wait, wait.

975
00:39:03.420 --> 00:39:04.320
You'll never guess.

976
00:39:04.520 --> 00:39:05.140
Wait, wait, wait.

977
00:39:05.160 --> 00:39:06.000
I want to try a guess.

978
00:39:06.400 --> 00:39:07.320
You can eat it.

979
00:39:07.560 --> 00:39:09.020
I thought you could eat it.

980
00:39:09.080 --> 00:39:10.320
I was going to say like Jell-O.

981
00:39:11.180 --> 00:39:11.860
Nestle's Quick.

982
00:39:12.640 --> 00:39:13.020
Oh.

983
00:39:13.540 --> 00:39:13.920
Yeah.

984
00:39:14.480 --> 00:39:16.000
That thickens it a little, I guess.

985
00:39:16.080 --> 00:39:16.300
Yeah.

986
00:39:16.300 --> 00:39:21.420
So our blood was all made by our special effects team led by Ron Nary.

987
00:39:21.840 --> 00:39:23.500
Had to make fakie blood that day.

988
00:39:23.640 --> 00:39:23.820
Fakie blood.

989
00:39:24.060 --> 00:39:30.240
Well, I thought the reveal of Hank when Michael comes to was one of the best moments.

990
00:39:30.460 --> 00:39:31.780
I laughed so hard.

991
00:39:31.940 --> 00:39:32.960
It was so perfect.

992
00:39:33.140 --> 00:39:33.620
It was so perfect.

993
00:39:33.620 --> 00:39:35.240
And then he calls the nurse a waitress.

994
00:39:35.360 --> 00:39:36.660
He's like so out of it.

995
00:39:36.860 --> 00:39:38.440
And he finds her glove.

996
00:39:38.680 --> 00:39:39.680
He does.

997
00:39:39.960 --> 00:39:43.480
And this starts his whole mission to find her.

998
00:39:43.920 --> 00:39:45.080
To return the glove.

999
00:39:45.260 --> 00:39:45.560
Yeah.

1000
00:39:45.560 --> 00:39:47.020
Like Cinderella's slipper.

1001
00:39:47.180 --> 00:39:47.560
I know.

1002
00:39:47.700 --> 00:39:48.460
It's really cute.

1003
00:39:49.000 --> 00:39:54.580
We have one more clip from Katie where she just shares her memories of her time on the show.

1004
00:39:54.720 --> 00:39:57.720
I asked her, anything stick out to you?

1005
00:39:57.900 --> 00:40:00.320
And Angela, wait until you hear what she says.

1006
00:40:00.460 --> 00:40:01.060
Oh, I can't wait.

1007
00:40:02.440 --> 00:40:07.900
I don't remember a ton of details about my time on set.

1008
00:40:07.900 --> 00:40:15.920
Except for that you guys were on your last day of like a very, very, very long cycle of shooting.

1009
00:40:15.960 --> 00:40:20.240
And everyone was just dead.

1010
00:40:20.780 --> 00:40:21.580
Tired.

1011
00:40:21.580 --> 00:40:24.720
And just ready for a hiatus.

1012
00:40:25.140 --> 00:40:28.300
So, um, that is what I remember.

1013
00:40:28.440 --> 00:40:29.420
But they were lovely.

1014
00:40:29.800 --> 00:40:31.380
Everyone was great.

1015
00:40:31.820 --> 00:40:40.520
But just like the talk was all about how this hiatus was just so needed.

1016
00:40:40.520 --> 00:40:42.140
So, that's what I remember.

1017
00:40:43.480 --> 00:40:46.580
That and, um, that you guys moved so quickly.

1018
00:40:46.920 --> 00:40:48.260
It was like the fasteSt.

1019
00:40:48.360 --> 00:40:50.520
I don't even know if I got lunch that day.

1020
00:40:50.640 --> 00:40:51.480
Like I showed up.

1021
00:40:51.760 --> 00:40:52.860
I did my scene.

1022
00:40:52.860 --> 00:40:55.920
And I, I'm pretty sure you guys banged me out.

1023
00:40:55.920 --> 00:40:57.520
And I didn't even get a free lunch.

1024
00:40:58.380 --> 00:40:59.100
All right.

1025
00:40:59.380 --> 00:41:01.940
This was, remember early on?

1026
00:41:02.260 --> 00:41:07.820
We had to do 18 episodes in a row so that we could create that hiatus for Steve to go

1027
00:41:07.820 --> 00:41:08.360
do a movie.

1028
00:41:08.520 --> 00:41:08.720
Yeah.

1029
00:41:09.100 --> 00:41:10.760
This was that 18th episode.

1030
00:41:11.020 --> 00:41:12.740
We were so wiped.

1031
00:41:13.180 --> 00:41:13.400
Yep.

1032
00:41:13.760 --> 00:41:16.260
18 weeks of 12 to 14 hour days.

1033
00:41:16.500 --> 00:41:16.700
Yeah.

1034
00:41:17.160 --> 00:41:22.280
And you guys, you know when you have that stretch of work where you leave work and it's

1035
00:41:22.280 --> 00:41:25.760
dark out and then you come back to work and it's still dark out.

1036
00:41:25.920 --> 00:41:26.480
You know what I mean?

1037
00:41:26.520 --> 00:41:27.600
Because you're there so early.

1038
00:41:27.940 --> 00:41:28.160
Yeah.

1039
00:41:28.320 --> 00:41:31.120
And you're just like, and you sort of all look at each other and joke and be like,

1040
00:41:31.660 --> 00:41:32.740
see you in a few hours.

1041
00:41:33.100 --> 00:41:34.220
There's a whole thing now.

1042
00:41:34.360 --> 00:41:35.220
It's called clopening.

1043
00:41:36.100 --> 00:41:36.500
Clopening?

1044
00:41:36.820 --> 00:41:37.220
Clopening.

1045
00:41:37.460 --> 00:41:42.760
And it's a lot of people who work in the service industry or in the food industry where you have

1046
00:41:42.760 --> 00:41:46.440
to close the restaurant and then like a few hours later you have to open it.

1047
00:41:46.580 --> 00:41:46.780
Yeah.

1048
00:41:47.040 --> 00:41:47.440
Clopening.

1049
00:41:47.760 --> 00:41:48.160
Clopening.

1050
00:41:48.360 --> 00:41:49.920
Well, we were in the clopening phase.

1051
00:41:50.020 --> 00:41:50.580
We were.

1052
00:41:50.760 --> 00:41:55.680
That is hilarious to me because I do remember like when we would wrap after a big stretch like that.

1053
00:41:55.920 --> 00:41:57.400
I would get like a cold.

