1816
01:12:41.940 --> 01:12:42.860
We got mail.

1817
01:12:43.180 --> 01:12:43.400
Okay.

1818
01:12:44.260 --> 01:12:44.920
Aiden M.

1819
01:12:45.320 --> 01:12:52.360
wrote in to say, why did Michael never get to find the lady who left her glove

1820
01:12:52.360 --> 01:12:53.620
in the blood drive van?

1821
01:12:53.760 --> 01:12:56.920
It has driven me crazy, even though he ends up with Holly.

1822
01:12:56.920 --> 01:12:58.620
And Diana P.

1823
01:12:58.880 --> 01:13:02.480
went on to say, why didn't this storyline continue?

1824
01:13:03.120 --> 01:13:07.220
I asked Katie about it because I was curious.

1825
01:13:07.680 --> 01:13:12.840
It just shows you how good of a job they did together in that scene that people wanted

1826
01:13:12.840 --> 01:13:16.280
to see more of the blood drive girl and Michael.

1827
01:13:16.620 --> 01:13:21.460
Well, the message boards after this episode aired were all for Glove Girl.

1828
01:13:21.460 --> 01:13:23.760
And here's what Katie had to say.

1829
01:13:24.500 --> 01:13:26.900
Oh, man, you guys.

1830
01:13:27.240 --> 01:13:38.920
So here is the thing about my experience is that when I auditioned, it was with the caveat

1831
01:13:38.920 --> 01:13:43.740
that it was a possible recurring character.

1832
01:13:45.560 --> 01:13:53.680
And so all I wanted was to perform well and to impress and to be asked back.

1833
01:13:54.100 --> 01:13:56.900
And it didn't happen.

1834
01:13:57.220 --> 01:13:58.320
It didn't happen.

1835
01:13:59.200 --> 01:14:02.180
And I'm sure they had their creative reasons.

1836
01:14:02.940 --> 01:14:07.440
But, oh, boy, I wanted nothing more.

1837
01:14:08.520 --> 01:14:10.620
But I'm happy with the time I got.

1838
01:14:11.180 --> 01:14:12.420
That's for sure.

1839
01:14:14.300 --> 01:14:18.460
So, I will tell you, story-wise, why Glove Girl did not come back.

1840
01:14:18.460 --> 01:14:23.220
It was not because we were not completely charmed by Katie and her performance.

1841
01:14:23.360 --> 01:14:24.460
No, she crushed it.

1842
01:14:24.640 --> 01:14:25.480
Clearly, yes.

1843
01:14:26.100 --> 01:14:27.600
Michael has a talking head.

1844
01:14:27.600 --> 01:14:29.980
And it's really written in this talking head.

1845
01:14:30.280 --> 01:14:37.080
He says that this is the first time since Holly that he's even considered getting back

1846
01:14:37.080 --> 01:14:38.400
into the dating marina.

1847
01:14:38.900 --> 01:14:39.460
Marina?

1848
01:14:39.700 --> 01:14:40.340
The marina.

1849
01:14:42.120 --> 01:14:43.800
Like Cupid's Sparrow.

1850
01:14:44.040 --> 01:14:44.160
Yeah.

1851
01:14:45.740 --> 01:14:53.960
And that was the story point of this episode, was not to introduce a new love interest for

1852
01:14:53.960 --> 01:14:54.300
Michael.

1853
01:14:54.480 --> 01:14:55.600
They ultimately decided.

1854
01:14:56.360 --> 01:14:57.960
They were toying with this idea.

1855
01:14:57.960 --> 01:15:05.340
But really, it was just for Michael to feel like he could connect with someone again.

1856
01:15:05.600 --> 01:15:09.520
But ultimately, they're going to keep him on this trajectory toward Holly.

1857
01:15:09.740 --> 01:15:16.640
But because of this storyline, he's not going to be kind of as broken when he does finally

1858
01:15:16.640 --> 01:15:17.460
reunite with her.

1859
01:15:17.560 --> 01:15:18.220
Does that make sense?

1860
01:15:18.220 --> 01:15:18.740
Yeah.

1861
01:15:19.040 --> 01:15:19.940
No, he's hopeful.

1862
01:15:20.320 --> 01:15:22.160
He's getting a little bit of his confidence back.

1863
01:15:22.260 --> 01:15:22.560
Yes.

1864
01:15:22.820 --> 01:15:23.680
And that's important.

1865
01:15:24.240 --> 01:15:24.580
Yeah.

1866
01:15:25.100 --> 01:15:27.060
Well, the whole gang is going to leave the building.

1867
01:15:27.480 --> 01:15:32.220
And Jenna, I just want you guys to know, when you watch us all exit, Mindy and I are just

1868
01:15:32.220 --> 01:15:33.200
having a conversation.

1869
01:15:33.480 --> 01:15:34.200
Yeah, I saw that.

1870
01:15:34.320 --> 01:15:35.540
I'm gesturing to my hair.

1871
01:15:35.540 --> 01:15:37.040
I don't know what we're talking about.

1872
01:15:37.040 --> 01:15:38.120
You're very animated.

1873
01:15:38.360 --> 01:15:38.960
Very animated.

1874
01:15:39.220 --> 01:15:43.320
And then I feel like they sort of let us know that we were on camera, because then I'd

1875
01:15:43.320 --> 01:15:46.300
go back to Angela Martin, and I'd do these little awkward waves goodbye.

1876
01:15:46.700 --> 01:15:49.440
But everyone is very pleasant and nice to one another.

1877
01:15:50.860 --> 01:15:53.640
Michael's Lonely Hearts party was kind of a success.

1878
01:15:54.160 --> 01:15:54.480
Yeah.

1879
01:15:54.720 --> 01:15:57.140
I mean, they were all sort of lonely together.

1880
01:15:57.440 --> 01:15:57.720
Yeah.

1881
01:15:58.060 --> 01:16:00.480
This episode ends with a great tag.

1882
01:16:00.800 --> 01:16:01.740
It's so funny.

1883
01:16:01.920 --> 01:16:02.840
Found it very funny.

1884
01:16:02.840 --> 01:16:09.020
And Stanley goes into the blood mobile, and he's got a little bandage on his arm.

1885
01:16:09.120 --> 01:16:11.340
He's got a cotton ball with a little bit of medical tape.

1886
01:16:11.520 --> 01:16:12.640
And he says, I'm so sorry.

1887
01:16:12.640 --> 01:16:15.820
I gave blood earlier, and I'm still feeling a little woozy.

1888
01:16:16.000 --> 01:16:17.000
Do you have a cookie?

1889
01:16:17.680 --> 01:16:19.240
Can I have one of those cookies?

1890
01:16:19.560 --> 01:16:19.880
Right.

1891
01:16:21.140 --> 01:16:24.180
And she says, you know what?

1892
01:16:24.420 --> 01:16:27.840
You have a cotton ball and medical tape, but we're using Band-Aids.

1893
01:16:27.980 --> 01:16:28.100
Yeah.

1894
01:16:28.180 --> 01:16:28.800
She's like, huh.

1895
01:16:29.360 --> 01:16:29.740
Weird.

1896
01:16:30.440 --> 01:16:32.800
And behind him, Phyllis walks up.

1897
01:16:33.180 --> 01:16:35.500
He's making a quick exit, and he just goes, Band-Aid.

1898
01:16:35.660 --> 01:16:36.880
And she's like, damn it.

1899
01:16:39.020 --> 01:16:44.000
And then Creed leaves the truck with his blood in a bag, or someone else's.

1900
01:16:44.060 --> 01:16:44.600
I'm not sure.

1901
01:16:44.860 --> 01:16:45.860
To go where?

1902
01:16:46.040 --> 01:16:46.840
To do what?

1903
01:16:47.020 --> 01:16:50.380
I don't know, but this is what Dwight has been worried about the whole episode.

1904
01:16:50.540 --> 01:16:51.000
I know.

1905
01:16:51.080 --> 01:16:51.980
Where is Dwight?

1906
01:16:52.840 --> 01:16:53.640
I don't know.

1907
01:16:54.200 --> 01:16:56.020
Well, that was blood drive, everybody.

1908
01:16:56.120 --> 01:16:57.720
That is blood drive, everyone.

1909
01:16:57.820 --> 01:16:58.860
I'm going to go home.

1910
01:16:58.860 --> 01:17:00.460
I'm going to put on different shoes.

1911
01:17:00.780 --> 01:17:01.820
Cool off your feet.

1912
